The fundamental problem with semantic prime languages was dealt with alread=
y by Aristotle (the system is either incomplete or circular), though not ex=
plicitly about language.  The various choices to take once the first proble=
m is overcome (either way) can be justified in various way;in the case {vru=
si 1}, both practicality and philosophy favor the prototype approach, but i=
t does lack precision. (blood tastes salty because it contains salt, after =
all).

